## indirect_alternatives
```json
[
  {
    "name": "Excel Spreadsheets with Carbon Templates",
    "why_used": "Low-cost, familiar tool for SMEs to manually calculate emissions, but lacks automation and actionable insights."
  },
  {
    "name": "Power BI Energy Dashboards",
    "why_used": "Provides visual analytics for energy usage but requires manual data entry and does not offer AI-driven recommendations."
  },
  {
    "name": "External Carbon Auditing Firms",
    "why_used": "Offers expert assessments and compliance support, yet is expensive and not scalable for frequent monitoring."
  },
  {
    "name": "Government Carbon Calculators",
    "why_used": "Free tools for basic emissions estimation, but limited in scope and integration with business operations."
  }
]
```

## status_quo
Small businesses currently rely on manual spreadsheets, generic energy dashboards, or external consultants to track and reduce carbon emissions. These methods are time-consuming, lack real-time data integration, and provide limited actionable insights, leading to suboptimal compliance and missed cost-saving opportunities.

